      <div type="clause" n="38.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 38.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="38.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="338" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ á swa man byð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_38-1.lnote.oe.16"/> mihtigra oððe maran hádes, swa scæl<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_38-1.lnote.oe.17"/> he deoppor for Gode ⁊ for worulde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_38-1.lnote.oe.18"/> unriht gebetan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="38.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="338" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ a swa man bið mihtigra oððe maran hades, swa sceal hé deoppor for Gode ⁊ for worulde unriht gebetan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="38.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="338" ed="#liebermann"/>And á swa man byð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_38-1.lnote.oe.5"/> mihtra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_38-1.lnote.oe.6"/> oððe maran hades, swa sceal he deoppor for Gode ⁊ for weorulde unriht gebetan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="38.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="339" ed="#liebermann"/>Semperque, sicut homo potentior est uel maioris ordinis, sic debet sollertius pro Deo et seculo quod iniustum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_38-1.lnote.oe.15"/> est emendare.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="38.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="339" ed="#liebermann"/>Et quanto quis potentior est uel maioris ordinis, tanto debet ille altius secundum Deum et seculum iniuriam patratam corrigere.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="38.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="194" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ a swa man bið mihtigra oððe maran hades, swa sceal hé deoppor for Gode ⁊ for worulde unriht gebetan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="276" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And a swa man byð mihtigra oððe maran hades, swa scæl he deoppor for Gode and for worulde unriht gebetan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="339" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_38-1.lnote.de.1"/> je mächtiger oder höheren Standes immer jemand ist, um so tiefer soll er Unrecht kirchlich und weltlich büssen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And the more powerful or the higher in rank anyone is, the more deeply must he atone for wrong before God and before the world.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_38-1.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="195" ed="#robertson"/>And in all cases, the greater a man is and the higher his rank, the more stringent shall be the amends which he shall be required to make to God and to men for lawless behaviour.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="467" ed="#whitelock"/>And ever as a man is mightier or of higher rank, he must atone the deeper both to God and to men for wrong-doing.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="277" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And always, the mightier a person is or the higher his rank, so must he do penance for his crimes all the more sincerely before God and the world.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="339">Can. Edg. Conf. 4</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd.</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="359"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_52">VI Atr 52</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 38:1: VI Atr 52  Conf. III</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="334"><label>recurs in later code</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_52">VI Atr 52–53</ref> <quote>Almost all these additions recurred in codes later drafted by Wulfstan for Cnut (n. 332: VI Atr 52–53, II Cn 38.1, II Cn 68.1–3)</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VI Atr 52.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 339, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_38-1.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">339</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">iustum <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">iustum Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_38-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">338</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">biþ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">biþ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_38-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">338</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sceal he deopor <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sceal he deopor Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_38-1.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">338</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ld <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ld Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_38-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">338</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">byd <hi rend="italic">A</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">byd A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_38-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">338</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mihtigra <hi rend="italic">Can. Edg.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mihtigra Can. Edg.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_38-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">208</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dieselbe homiletische Stelle wird <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 68, 1a benutzt und VI Atr 52, wo Anm. <hi rend="italic">vgl</hi>.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The same homiletic passage is used <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 68, 1a and in VI Atr 52, where <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> the note</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_38-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. VI Atr. 52; II Cn. 68, 1 <hi rend="italic">a</hi>.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
